/-!
# The orthogonality of the escape correction at `L₁ = K`

This file proves `Work.GrunwaldEscapeCore.L1Korth.alpha_fixes_L1K`: in the situation of the
escape-form Grünwald theorem with `L₁ = K`, `g = 0`, the Artin symbol
`α = art (fracIdele (tFreePart T' a))` fixes pointwise every element of `M` that lies in `L`.

The route is the "class-group" one: the `T'`-free part `𝔡 = tFreePart T' a` of the divisor of the
Grünwald element `a` is shown to be an idèlic norm from `F = M ⊓ L` (its class lies in
`N_{F/↥K} C_F`), and the norm-class form of the local-global compatibility
(`N4Escape.restrictNormalHom_artinMap_kills_normClassSubgroup_of_modulus`) then says that `α`
restricts trivially to `F`.  Concretely:

* `idele_decomposition_tFreePart` writes `(a)ᵥ = P · 𝔡 · u` with `P = ∏_{𝔭 ∈ T'} e_𝔭(a)` the
  `T'`-part of `(a)ᵥ` and `u ∈ powTIdeles`;
* `mk u` lies in `gesU ⊆ gesUPow ↥K p T' = N_{M/↥K} C_M ⊆ N_{F/↥K} C_F` (norm transitivity, since
  `F ≤ M`);
* each `mk (e_𝔭(a))`, `𝔭 ∈ T'`, lies in `N_{F/↥K} C_F`: either the orthogonality clause
  `h A ≡ 0` holds at a place `A | 𝔭`, in which case `a` is a local `p`-th power at `𝔭` (local
  Kummer dictionary) so that `e_𝔭(a)` is a `p`-th power in `C_↥K ⊆ N_{M/↥K}C_M`; or the second
  clause holds, in which case `𝔭` splits completely in `F/↥K` and the local factor is a norm.
-/

